Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:46:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Extend status dashboard to the full discovered coin
 universe

scripts/generate_status_dashboard.py rendered exactly two symbol cards
(BTC/USD, ETH/USD) via a hardcoded SYMBOLS tuple, matching the old
BTC/ETH-only pipeline. Now that .13-.19/.23 evaluate the full
discovered Alpaca crypto universe under the required-vs-optional
symbol pattern, the dashboard needs to show every symbol a cycle
actually reported on, not just the required pair.

- Renamed SYMBOLS -> REQUIRED_SYMBOLS (BTC/USD, ETH/USD): these are
  now the *floor*, always rendered even with no data yet, rather than
  the ceiling.
- render() now computes discovered_symbols as the union of the
  signal/safety/spec decisions dict keys plus REQUIRED_SYMBOLS, and
  builds one card per discovered symbol. symbol_card() already looked
  up each source independently via .get(...), so an optional symbol
  missing from one upstream source (e.g. present in signal but not yet
  in safety) still renders cleanly with dashes for the missing pieces
  instead of crashing -- no logic change was needed there.
- Updated the static header text that hardcoded "(BTC/USD, ETH/USD)"
  to describe the full discovered universe with BTC/USD, ETH/USD
  called out as always-required.
- This is a read-only, report-only change: the dashboard has no
  ability to place an order and nothing here touches .19's
  execution_authorized boundary or .23's direction allowlists.

Added tests/test_generate_status_dashboard.py (7 tests, loaded via
importlib like the other script-style tests in this repo): no-data
placeholder renders no cards, required symbols always render even
with empty upstream data, an optional discovered symbol (e.g.
AVAX/USD) gets its own card, an optional symbol missing from some but
not all upstream sources doesn't crash, a required symbol absent from
every upstream source for a given cycle still renders, the header no
longer hardcodes exactly two symbols, and a symbol_card() smoke test
with no upstream data at all.

Full suite: 88 passed (pytest, excluding the two Alpaca-credential
tests that fail in this sandbox for unrelated reasons) plus the
existing 11/11 .22 adapter contract test, unaffected by this change.

This is the tenth and final file of Phase 1 (BTC/ETH-required +
mirror short candidate + full discovered coin universe support),
authorized by Martin's "Start building :)".

